<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George Carteret</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1610–<a href="/years/1680">1680</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Sir George Carteret</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sir George Carteret was a Jersey-born royalist naval officer who held Jersey for Charles I and became a courtier after the Restoration. In 1664 he and John Berkeley received the land between the Hudson and Delaware rivers, named <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-jersey">New Jersey</a> after his island; after its division in 1674 he held East Jersey as proprietor.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-carteret.jpg" alt="George Carteret" width="200" height="279" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SirGeorgeCarteret.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
